PARITY MODEL: the closest web sibling is AIGeofenceAwareAutomationSuggestions (0020) — the
draft-capture + onApply pattern. Two faithful deltas from that sibling, both dictated by the web
source AISignalExplorerNlFilter.tsx:
  (a) the capture guard runs `parseSignalFilterDraft` which keeps the draft ONLY when
      `data.status === 'ok'` AND the inner filter normalises (vehicle_id number, signals string[],
      range_preset string, per_page number) — it NEVER inspects `ev.ok` (verdict carried by status),
      so there is no "rejected proposal" surface (a non-ok status is dropped);
  (b) AISignalExplorerNlFilter has NO vehicle-change cleanup effect (unlike geofence), so a vehicle
      change updates scope WITHOUT cancelling the stream or clearing the captured draft — mirrored in
      `SignalExplorerFilterModel.apply(input:)` and asserted by testVehicleChangeKeepsDraftAndPrompt.

